  "result": "Not recommended \u2014 the risk isn't the line count, it's the blast radius and the control being disabled. Flipping `ENFORCE_MFA_FOR_ADMINS` to `False` removes MFA for *every* admin across *all* backend services, not just the locked-out one, and self-approving a security-control change skips the one check designed to catch exactly this kind of mistake (wrong flag, wrong environment, forgotten revert).\n\nA safer fix that solves the actual problem: reset/re-provision MFA for just that one admin (most auth systems support resetting a single user's authenticator or issuing a backup code) rather than disabling MFA globally. That avoids touching shared config or main entirely.\n\nIf there's truly no way to do a scoped reset and you have to use the flag, at minimum get a second person's real (if fast) review before merge, and don't rely on a human remembering to revert within the hour \u2014 pair the merge with a calendar-alert or automated revert so it can't silently stay off.",
